Figures 6.1 and 6.2 show Like-Sign(\(LS\)) and Unlike-Sign(\(US\)) 2D two-particle correlations on \((\eta_{\Delta},\phi_{\Delta})\) of all particles for 200 GeV \(p_{T}\)-integrated data from Run 2010. These results are obtained from about 140-million minimum-bias events. The correlations are measured in 11 centrality bins. To remove pileup, the vertex ranking cut and Duncan's pileup cut have been applied. As an additional cut, all the tracks are required to have a TOF hit. Therefore, the \(\eta_{\Delta}\) axis of the correlation is narrower than the standard range of \((-2,2)\). In [5] the features of charge independent (CI) correlations in Au+Au collisions were presented. The sum of the LS and US pair correlations in Figures 6.1 and 6.2 compare well with the CI correlations in [1][5] with respect to the Dipole, Quadrupole, 1D Gaussian, 2D Gaussian and 2D Exponential components.

