### Factorization

The measured \(v_{2}^{2}\) is a function of the type of particle-pair and the \(p_{T}(y_{T})\) of each particle in the pair. Factorization assumes that \(v_{2}^{2}\) can be decomposed into factors as shown in Equation 6.11

\[v_{2,ij}^{2}(p_{Ti},p_{Tj})=v_{2i}(p_{Ti})v_{2j}(p_{Tj}), \tag{6.11}\]

